<think>
Okay, I need to figure out whether Mo3tthi can force a win in this game. Let me try to understand the problem step by step.

So, there are K pockets. Each pocket has a certain number of biscuits initially (N_i) and a capacity (M_i). Mo3tthi starts first. They take turns performing operations on a pocket. Each operation can be either:

1. Stroking the selected pocket: This increases the number of biscuits in the pocket by 1. But if after this operation, the number of biscuits exceeds the capacity, it's not allowed. Wait, but initially, N_i is less than or equal to M_i. So when you stroke, you can do it as long as adding 1 doesn't exceed M_i. Wait, no. Wait, if you choose a pocket, then you can perform either of two operations. Let me re-read:

When you choose a pocket, you perform one of the two operations only once. But if the operation would make the number of biscuits in the pocket exceed the capacity, you can't perform that operation. 

